1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,564
Open Client briefs in ANC Presentations. This is
the shared starting point

2
00:00:05,564 --> 00:00:10,778
for sales, design, and proposal preparation. We
will use a clearly labeled

3
00:00:10,778 --> 00:00:13,385
training brief to show the workflow.

4
00:00:14,217 --> 00:00:17,651
Enter the client, venue, audience, and meeting
goal once.

5
00:00:17,651 --> 00:00:20,703
Add the deadline and choose the brief owner.

6
00:00:20,703 --> 00:00:24,901
Everyone reads the same context, instead of
preparing from separate messages.

7
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:29,820
Search by account or venue to connect the real
CRM opportunity.

8
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:32,805
Select the right record, then save the brief.

9
00:00:32,805 --> 00:00:37,282
The opportunity stays in the CRM; the brief
connects the preparation around

10
00:00:37,282 --> 00:00:37,655
it.

11
00:00:38,483 --> 00:00:42,326
Link an existing presentation, or choose an
approved sales kit and create

12
00:00:42,326 --> 00:00:46,169
a presentation from this brief. The kit uses the
saved client details

13
00:00:46,169 --> 00:00:47,130
and meeting goal.

14
00:00:47,950 --> 00:00:50,796
Open the presentation and review its sections.

15
00:00:50,796 --> 00:00:55,676
Choose Share, then Go live, create link and
copy, to publish the

16
00:00:55,676 --> 00:01:00,149
saved client version. Return to the shared brief
to finish preparation.

17
00:01:00,950 --> 00:01:05,044
Add the showroom's published client link, then
select the supporting files from

18
00:01:05,044 --> 00:01:09,137
the existing library. Use the published project
link, so the team can

19
00:01:09,137 --> 00:01:12,548
check the venue material that the client will
actually see.

20
00:01:13,350 --> 00:01:17,815
Assign each deliverable to a person. Designers
can see the creative they

21
00:01:17,815 --> 00:01:22,279
need to prepare, and Natalia can see what is
ready for proposal

22
00:01:22,279 --> 00:01:25,628
assembly. Add production notes, and mark
completed deliverables ready.

23
00:01:26,450 --> 00:01:30,003
Choose named brief editors and handoff
approvers, then save.

24
00:01:30,003 --> 00:01:34,741
Editors prepare the brief. Approvers decide when
it is ready for sales.

25
00:01:34,741 --> 00:01:37,505
These permissions govern the brief and handoff;

26
00:01:37,505 --> 00:01:40,269
linked applications keep their own access
settings.

27
00:01:41,083 --> 00:01:46,108
Send the completed brief to Review. An approver
selects Approve for sales.

28
00:01:46,108 --> 00:01:51,133
The platform checks the published presentation
and showroom, and records the approved

29
00:01:51,133 --> 00:01:54,902
versions. Missing or changed material must be
resolved first.

30
00:01:55,717 --> 00:02:00,171
Copy approved client links to collect the
presentation and showroom links together.

31
00:02:00,171 --> 00:02:04,626
Internal notes stay inside the workspace. After
sending those links yourself, enter

32
00:02:04,626 --> 00:02:07,596
the recipient and record the handoff as Shared.

33
00:02:07,596 --> 00:02:09,823
This does not send a message.

34
00:02:10,650 --> 00:02:14,873
Revision history shows who saved, reviewed,
approved, and recorded the handoff.

35
00:02:14,873 --> 00:02:17,944
Open an earlier revision to inspect its context.

36
00:02:17,944 --> 00:02:22,552
Reopen for preparation when the brief needs
changes, then review the updated

37
00:02:22,552 --> 00:02:23,319
material again.
